{
  "card": "PLAN-41",
  "description": "PLAN-41: what the Acceptance job runs. Every class of HRManagement.AcceptanceTests appears exactly once, in lab[], in prodLike[] (class, required, group) or in excluded[] (class or Class.Method, reason, ownerPlan, reviewBy). Exclude only for an environment CI cannot provide, never because a class is red. order[] is the order of the stages; stack is the stack a stage needs; ciOnly stages read the results of the CI job of the same commit, so they do not run on the owner\u0027s machine. A class in the isolated group stops or recreates containers and runs alone, in its own test process (P-7). PLAN-42: a stage with composeFiles applies them on the running stack, recreating the services in recreate; its classes also run alone, and the stack is torn down before its next use, so such a stage comes last on its stack. A class in a trx that is not listed here fails the job. PLAN-66: stageJobs[] groups order[] into the parallel jobs of ci.yml; every entry of order[] belongs to one of them. waitFor names the jobs whose evidence a stage must read: its class looks at the folders of the run. metaRule: the stage that runs on demand (D-QA-66-1) and what its classes read; the guard and the validator accept not run by rule only for the classes of that stage.",
